# 57. Final Concept

The easiest way for students to remember JOINs is:

```text
              WHY?
               │
      Data is in multiple tables
               │
               ↓
             JOIN
               │
      How are they related?
               │
               ↓
              ON
               │
               ↓
       Which rows should match?
               │
               ↓
        Combined result
```

The key idea is:

> **A JOIN connects related data stored in different tables.**

Once students understand this, SQL becomes much easier because they can stop thinking of tables as isolated objects and start thinking about the **relationships between data**.
